Findings: [minor] LibKa0sSkinTester tests/test_showroom_widgets.lua:98-106 (with modules/ShowroomWidgets.lua:680-691): Nothing tests the LK-06a part of the Library widgets section. No test checks that the drag handle label, the autocomplete rows, the chart tick labels or the menu rows are drawn in the skin's body face, or that Ignore fonts gives their template face back. No test checks that the section stays skinned while Ignore settings panel is ticked (D-01). The test named 'owned by this addon' only asserts handleSpec.owner. Proven by mutation: deleting `owner = addonName` from the Autocomplete and LineChart calls leaves all 569 tests green, so those two samples could silently stop showing the newly skinned fonts. Only the owner's in-client run of SHOW-21 would catch it. | [minor] LibKa0sSkinTester docs/smoke-tests.md PANEL-11 (lines ~85-93): PANEL-11 asks the owner to check drawer heads on the tester's settings pages: the chevron in Glass's arrow color, the label in Glass's body face and Oxanium under Ka0s Default, with failure if 'a drawer label in Friz Quadrata'. The tester's pages have no drawer. settings/OptionsSetup.lua:148-149 stubs H.Drawer as a no-op with no call site, and the library builds drawers only through a host's O.Drawer. Those clauses cannot be carried out, so PANEL-11 could be recorded as passed without anything being checked. The nav-rail and tooltip clauses are valid. | [nit] LibKa0sSkinTester tests/test_showroom_widgets.lua:139-146: The test 'the copy window opens owned by this addon' asserts only that the window shows and has a resizeGrip. A copy window has a grip whether or not it has an owner, so the grip's icon.grip tint, which SHOW-23 and the section header claim, is not pinned. The test goes red without `addonName` only because the window then fails to build.
Fix round: I checked both findings and fixed both. I rejected neither.

1 (tests): Confirmed. Three cases were added to /mnt/d/Profile/Users/Tushar/Documents/GIT/LibKa0sSkinTester/tests/test_showroom_widgets.lua. They run under the paint recorder and a LibSharedMedia stand-in.
- The chart's tick labels and the autocomplete rows are Skin.painted records owned by LibKa0sSkinTester, made through S.Font and drawn in the owner's body font object.
- NS.ApplySkinIgnore(nil, true) gives each one its template back (GameFontDisableSmall or GameFontHighlightSmall). Unticking it brings the body face back.
- NS.ApplySkinIgnore(true, nil) under Glass keeps the drawer and nav hover art and the resize grip desaturated and tinted (list.hoverArt, icon.grip), and the fonts stay skinned (D-01).

To make the give-back visible I added a file-local mock extension, modelTemplateFonts. A FontString made from a template now answers that template from GetFontObject until a face is set, as the client does. The base mock answered nil, so P.unfont had nothing to restore. I re-ran the reviewer's mutation (removing owner = addonName from Autocomplete and LineChart): all three new cases go red. docs/test-cases.md was regenerated (Total 571) and the README badge moved from 568 to 571.

2 (PANEL-11): Confirmed, and the problem is wider than reported. The nav-rail clause also cannot be carried out: O.NavRail, like O.Drawer, is drawn only when a host calls it, the tester never calls either, and settings/OptionsSetup.lua stubs both with "no page here draws a rail" and "no call site here". In /mnt/d/Profile/Users/Tushar/Documents/GIT/LibKa0sSkinTester/docs/smoke-tests.md, PANEL-11 now keeps only the row tooltip title (white under Glass, from gtip.value) and its give-back when Ignore settings panel is ticked. For LK-06c's hover art and chevron it points to SHOW-22. Before this run, the drawer label's body face was checked only by PANEL-11's dropped drawer clauses. It now has headless coverage only, from the existing paint("Drawer", ...) path and no new test, because SHOW-22 does not cover it. Nothing was pushed, tagged or merged. The branch is still feat/2026-10-30-skin-library-followups and the tree is clean.
